	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_icon_section_home"><![CDATA[Shown when someone adds the site to a phone's home screen, and on Android's launch screen while the site opens. Use a square image with some space and a background around the symbol.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_icon_section_tab"><![CDATA[Shown in browser tabs, bookmarks and history. Browsers that read SVG use the SVG icon, the others favicon.ico.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_icon_upload_icon"><![CDATA[A 32×32 .ico file.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_icon_upload_icon_android"><![CDATA[192×192.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_icon_upload_icon_android_splash"><![CDATA[512×512.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_icon_upload_icon_apple"><![CDATA[180×180. iOS fills transparent areas with black, so give it a background colour.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_icon_upload_icon_svg"><![CDATA[An .svg file. It can switch colours for dark mode with a prefers-color-scheme style.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_inj_section_body"><![CDATA[Added to every page of the site, right before <code>&lt;/body&gt;</code>. Use it for scripts that load after the content, such as chat widgets.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_inj_section_head"><![CDATA[Added to every page of the site, right before <code>&lt;/head&gt;</code>. Use it for meta tags, site verification, fonts, styles and analytics.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_logo_code"><![CDATA[Draws the logo from SVG markup in place of the default image. An uploaded image comes first.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_logo_section"><![CDATA[Shown in the header on wide screens.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_logo_text"><![CDATA[Read by screen readers, and shown in the header when there is no logo image. Leave empty to use the site name.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_mark_code"><![CDATA[Draws the mark from SVG markup in place of the default image. An uploaded image comes first.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_mark_section"><![CDATA[The compact symbol, shown in the header on phones and tablets.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_page_type_application"><![CDATA[A menu down the side and a slim bar on top, like an app.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_page_type_standard"><![CDATA[The header and site menu across the top, the footer at the bottom.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_page_type_wo_hf"><![CDATA[Only the page content: no header, menus or footer.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_pwa_background_color"><![CDATA[Fills the screen behind the icon while the app starts. Defaults to white.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_pwa_description"><![CDATA[One or two sentences about the site. Some install prompts show it.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_pwa_name"><![CDATA[Shown when installing and in the list of apps. Defaults to the site name.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_pwa_preview_home"><![CDATA[The icon and short name.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_pwa_preview_launch"><![CDATA[Shown while the app starts.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_pwa_preview_window"><![CDATA[The title bar in the window color.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_pwa_section_app"><![CDATA[People can add the site to their home screen or install it from the browser. It then opens in a window of its own, like an app. Leave a field empty to use the default it shows. The app icon comes from <a href="{0}">Icon</a>.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_pwa_section_sw"><![CDATA[A service worker is a small script the browser keeps for the site. It saves the site styles, scripts and icons on the device, so pages open faster, and it can show an offline page when there is no connection.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_pwa_short_name"><![CDATA[Shown under the icon on the home screen, where about 12 characters fit. Defaults to the app name, shortened.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_pwa_sw_cache"><![CDATA[One address per line, on this site or full. They are saved when the service worker installs, along with the site styles, scripts and icons, which it keeps anyway.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_pwa_sw_enable"><![CDATA[When you change the site styles or scripts, visitors get the new ones the next time they open the site.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_pwa_sw_offline"><![CDATA[Shown instead of the browser error when there is no connection: an address on this site, such as page.php?i=about. Leave it empty to use the browser page.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_pwa_theme_color"><![CDATA[Colors the app title bar and, on phones, the status bar. Defaults to the color your template sets.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_settings_section_layout"><![CDATA[Where the header, menus and footer go around the content of a page. Pages with a layout of their own in <a href="{0}">Pages</a> keep it; all the others use the ones below.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_settings_section_template"><![CDATA[The template draws the whole site: its header, menus, colors and fonts. Everyone sees this one unless they pick another enabled template themselves.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_splash_section_apps"><![CDATA[Code for one app only. An empty field uses the page code above. The apps draw the forms, the logo and the illustration with their own components, and leave out scripts and anything marked <code>data-site-only</code>. The iOS and Android apps show text, headings, lists and links, without styles or layout. Add <code>&lt;neo-slot name="social_login"&gt;&lt;/neo-slot&gt;</code> for the social sign-in buttons alone.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_splash_section_code"><![CDATA[HTML of the splash. These placeholders are filled in when it is shown: <code>__logo__</code> the site logo, <code>__illustration__</code> the splash illustration, <code>__join_form_in_box__</code> and <code>__login_form_in_box__</code> the sign-up and sign-in forms in a box, <code>__join_form__</code> and <code>__login_form__</code> the same forms without one, <code>__join_link__</code> and <code>__login_link__</code> their addresses, <code>{site_title}</code> the site name. The apps show this code too, unless App code below has their own, and leave out elements with the <code>data-site-only</code> attribute.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_splash_section_landing"><![CDATA[Guests who open the home page see the splash instead. Members who are signed in still see the home page. Turn it on for the site and for each app. Where an app's splash is off, its guests see the home page blocks from Page builder. The splash is not the launch screen the iOS and Android apps show while they start, which comes from Icon.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_splash_section_preview"><![CDATA[How guests see the splash on the site. Preview changes shows the code from the editor before you save it.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_tmpl_section_list"><![CDATA[A template draws the whole site: its header, menus, colors and fonts. These are the templates installed and turned on. Preview one to see it below, or open the site with it to try the real pages.]]></string_add>
	<string_add name="_adm_dsg_inf_tmpl_section_preview"><![CDATA[The real site in the template, on the page and at the screen size you pick. You see it signed in, as yourself, and links in it keep the template. Nothing changes for anyone else.]]></string_add>
